There is a bug in this debounce that ships in our snippets doc. Reproduce it with a failing test first, then fix it.

function debounce(fn, wait) {
  let t;
  return function (args) {
    clearTimeout(t);
    t = setTimeout(() => fn(args), wait);
  };
}

Set up /workspace/fix-debounce with vitest and fake timers. Write a test demonstrating that multiple arguments and the this binding are lost (call through an object method with two args and assert what the callee receives) and watch it fail against the code above copied verbatim into src/debounce.js. Then fix the implementation (rest args, apply with the captured this) without changing the public shape, and add a cancel method. Finish with the full suite green under npx vitest run, and keep the original failing expectations as the regression test.

tools_list = await mcp.list_tools("tools")
for t in tools_list:
    print(t["name"], t["inputSchema"])

